+<p><small>Matched neutral-grey studio views. Drag the slider or use its arrow keys. The production-camera option uses the unchanged camera profile over the diagnostic studio, not an actual race scene. “Mobile” here identifies the desktop renderer; it is not a device test.</small></p>
+<div class="grid"><figure><a id="before-link" href="before-native/full-rear-quarter.png"><img id="before-whole" src="before-native/full-rear-quarter.png" alt="Complete before view"></a><figcaption>Before · source-matched task-start model</figcaption></figure><figure><a id="after-link" href="native/full-rear-quarter.png"><img id="after-whole" src="native/full-rear-quarter.png" alt="Complete revised view"></a><figcaption>After · revised model, same pose and paint</figcaption></figure></div>
+<p><a href="app-native/garage-1280.png">Actual Garage</a> · <a href="app-native/model-rear.png">Actual rear view</a> · <a href="app-native/race.png">Actual gameplay</a> · <a href="model-native/electric-headlights.png">Headlights</a> · <a href="report.json">Commands and evidence</a> · <a href="../electric-design-review-2026-10-26/comparison.html">Original EV comparison review</a></p>
+<p><small>Fictional vehicle, original authored game geometry. Reference manufacturers remain design references outside the game assets. Reload the project/game to see the new prepared model in an existing session.</small></p>
